<title>USA: Swift says is defendant in gov't action.</title>
<headline>Swift says is defendant in gov't action.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swift Transportation Co Inc said the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission is seeking action against the company's policy of having new drivers trained by experienced drivers of the same sex.</p>
<p>Swift said that if the EEOC action is successful, it would require drivers of the opposite sex to share about 40 square feet of sleeping facilities in its trucks.</p>
<p>&quot;This policy was adopted by Swift to prevent sexual harassment in its training program. Swift believes that the EEOC action is without merit,&quot; the company said in a statement Friday. &quot;Swift will vigorously defend its policy.&quot;</p>
<p>Swift is the fourth largest publicly-held national truckload carrier in the United States.</p>
</text>
